    "background_story": "Brian was a well-known artist in the local community, celebrated for his vibrant and eclectic paintings. However, as his fame grew, so did concerns about his creative process. Critics began to notice that his work bore striking similarities to that of lesser-known artists from marginalized communities. It became clear that Brian had a habit of appropriating their styles, techniques, and even specific pieces, passing them off as his own. Despite the backlash, Brian continued to profit from his appropriative art, claiming that he was simply 'paying homage' to his inspirations. The art community was divided, with some defending his right to creative freedom and others condemning his lack of cultural sensitivity and respect for the original creators.",
